{
  "intent": "check_and_fix",
  "intent_description": "Restore IP reachability from host in 192.168.0.0/24 (source 192.168.0.162) to destination 172.16.0.12 (ping timeouts). Impact: host cannot reach destination. Desired outcome: pings to 172.16.0.12 succeed from router1's perspective and normal routing (no routing loop) is restored.",
  "target": "router1",
  "diagnosis": {
    "initial_condition": "Source host (192.168.0.162) cannot reach 172.16.0.12 (25 pings, 0 successes). Pre-remediation device state shows both router1 and router3 have static routes for 172.16.0.0/24 pointing at each other, creating a routing loop for that destination.",
    "root_causes": [
      {
        "type": "configuration",
        "cause": "Conflicting/static routes on router1 and router3 caused a routing loop for 172.16.0.0/24",
        "evidence": [
          "R1 running-config contains static route 172.16.0.0/255.255.255.0 next-hop 10.0.0.9 (get_running_config router1)",
